# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What is deliberately NOT in this repository, and why.
#
# Three kinds of thing are ignored: machine-generated output, files too large
# to version, and secrets. Every rule below says which it is. If you add one,
# say why too - a bare pattern is a rule nobody can ever safely delete.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- generated: javascript -------------------------------------------------
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local
*.tsbuildinfo
.vite

# --- generated: python -----------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- editor / OS -----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.=.swp

# --- local agent tooling (machine-specific state, not project config) ------
.claude-flow/
.claude/proven-config.json
.claude/.proven-config-version

# ===========================================================================
# SECRETS - nothing below this line may ever be committed
# ===========================================================================

# Camera credentials live here.
engine/.env

# Kaggle API token. The models/knife detection/ folder is not currently on
# disk; the rule stays because if the folder ever comes back, so does the key.
models/knife detection/kaggle.json

# Roboflow training scripts. Removed from the repo and purged from history:
# three of them had a live API key typed into the source. Keep these rules
# even though the folder is gone - they are what stops `git add -A` from
# putting the key back if the folder is ever restored from a backup.
models/knife detection/train_knife_model_colab.py
models/knife detection/train_knife_model_kaggle_colab.py
models/knife detection/train_knife_model_merged.py
models/knife detection/train_knife_model_v2_combined.py
models/knife detection/train_knife_model_v3_custom.py

# ===========================================================================
# TOO LARGE TO VERSION - tracked out of band. See the README in each folder
# for what is supposed to be there and where to get it.
# ===========================================================================

# --- runtime data: database, extracted clips, captured footage -------------
engine/data/

# --- model weights (~6 GB) -------------------------------------------------
# models/MODELS.md and models/README.md ARE tracked - they are the record of
# what is supposed to be in the folder.
models/*.pt
models/*.pth
models/*.onnx
models/*.engine
models/*.weights
models/*.safetensors

# Generated per-model sidecars - regenerate with engine/tools/audit_models.py
models/*_pt.yaml
models/*_pth.yaml
models/*_onnx.yaml
models/*_engine.yaml

# --- datasets (owner-supplied, ~200 MB) ------------------------------------
# The read truth CSV is the EXCEPTION: human-confirmed evidence must be
# versioned. See datasets/README.md.
datasets/*/
!datasets/README.md
!datasets/*/plate_truth.csv

# --- vendored projects: their bulk, not their source -----------------------
# vendor/README.md explains what each of these is. Their SOURCE is tracked;
# their weights and captured media are not.
vendor/bag-tracker/
vendor/gate-anpr/**/*.pt

# Training clips of real people - never commit. Consent and retention for
# footage of minors is an open question (docs/PLAN.md D1), and a repository
# is the one place footage can never be withdrawn from.
**/knife_clips/
*.mp4

# ===========================================================================
# LITTER - accidents from redirected shell commands ('> $OUT', '> 118').
# Cleaned out 1 Sep 2026; these rules stop them coming back.
# ===========================================================================
/$OUT
/$TMP_LOG
/[0-9]
/[0-9][0-9]
/[0-9][0-9][0-9]
_to_delete/
.speckit-init.zip
